==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
Possibly from the instrumental interrogative {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hwī||how, with what}}, with the initial h- replaced by the þ- from the forms of {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*sa}}.

===Conjunction===
'''því'''

# [[because]], [[for]], [[since]]
#* Colossians 3:9
#*: ''Ljúgið ekki hver að öðrum, '''því''' þér hafið afklæðst hinum gamla manni með gjörðum hans.''
#*:: Do not lie to each other, '''since''' you have taken off your old self with its practices.

====Derived terms====
* [[af því að]], [[því að]] (because)
* [[því aðeins að]] (only if, on the condition that)

===Pronoun===
'''því'''  {{context|personal|lang=is}}

# dative of the word [[það]]

====Declension====
{{Icelandic personal pronouns}}

===Adverb===
'''því...því'''

# [[the]]...[[the]] (when comparing)
#: ''en '''því''' meira sem hann blés, '''því''' þéttara vafði ferðamaðurinn kápunni að sér''
#:: ''but '''the''' more he blew, '''the''' tighter the traveller wrapped his coat around himself''

====Derived terms====
* [[því miður]]

